# Migrating Flat Pulumi Program to ComponentResource (No Replacement)

## The Core Problem

Wrapping resources in a ComponentResource changes every resource's URN, because URNs include the parent chain. Pulumi would see `urn:pulumi:prod::app::aws:s3/bucket:Bucket` become `urn:pulumi:prod::app::pkg:index:WebApp$aws:s3/bucket:Bucket` → **delete + create**.

**Fix:** pass the old flat URN via `aliases` so Pulumi treats each resource as "same resource, renamed."

---

## Step 0 — Original flat program (`index.ts`, before)

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config();

const cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster("cluster", {
  roleArn: /* ... */,
  vpcConfig: { subnetIds: /* ... */ },
});

const nodeGroup = new aws.eks.NodeGroup("nodes", {
  clusterName: cluster.name,
  nodeRoleArn: /* ... */,
  instanceTypes: [cfg.require("instanceType")],
  scalingConfig: { desiredSize: cfg.getNumber("nodeCount"), minSize: 1, maxSize: 10 },
});

const bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket("assets", {
  versioning: { enabled: true },
  serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: { rule: { applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } } },
});
// ... RDS, IAM role, secret
```

## Step 1 — The ComponentResource

```typescript
// component.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as awsx from "@pulumi/awsx";

export interface WebAppArgs {
  vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
  subnetIds: pulumi.Input<pulumi.Input<string>[]>;
  instanceType: pulumi.Input<string>;   // t3.medium / t3.large
  nodeCount: pulumi.Input<number>;      // 2 / 4
  dbInstanceClass: pulumi.Input<string>;// db.t3.micro / db.t3.medium
  multiAz: boolean;
  certArn?: pulumi.Input<string>;       // prod only
}

export class WebApp extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public readonly bucketArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
  public readonly dbSecretArn: pulumi.Output<string>;

  constructor(name: string, args: WebAppArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
    super("pkg:index:WebApp", name, {}, opts);

    // -- EKS ------------------------------------------------------------
    const cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster(`${name}-cluster`,
      {
        roleArn: /* existing cluster role arn lookup or import */,
        vpcConfig: { subnetIds: args.subnetIds },
      },
      // KEY MOVE: alias to the old flat resource identity
      { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:eks/cluster:Cluster" }] },
    );

    const nodes = new aws.eks.NodeGroup(`${name}-nodes`,
      {
        clusterName: cluster.name,
        nodeRoleArn: /* ... */,
        instanceTypes: [args.instanceType],
        scalingConfig: { desiredSize: args.nodeCount, minSize: 1, maxSize: 10 },
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:eks/nodeGroup:NodeGroup" }] },
    );

    // -- S3 -------------------------------------------------------------
    const bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(`${name}-assets`,
      {
        versioning: { enabled: true },
        serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
          rule: { applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } },
        },
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:s3/bucket:Bucket" }] },
    );

    // -- RDS ------------------------------------------------------------
    const db = new aws.rds.Instance(`${name}-db`,
      {
        instanceClass: args.dbInstanceClass,
        engine: "postgres",
        multiAz: args.multiAz,
        storageEncrypted: true,
        deletionProtection: true,
        backupRetentionPeriod: 14,
        publiclyAccessible: false,
        skipFinalSnapshot: false,
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:rds/instance:Instance" }] },
    );

    // Secret handed off via ConfigSecret-style secret output, never plaintext.
    const connStr = pulumi.all([db.address, db.username, db.password]).apply(
      ([addr, user, pass]) => `postgres://${user}:${pass}@${addr}:5432/app`);
    this.dbSecretArn = pulumi.createSecret(connStr);

    // IAM least-privilege service role (trusts OIDC for prod)
    const role = new aws.iam.Role(`${name}-svc-role`, {
      assumeRolePolicy: /* OIDC trust policy for prod / programmatic for dev */,
      managedPolicyArns: [],
    }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:iam/role:Role" }] });

    const policy = new aws.iam.RolePolicy(`${name}-svc-policy`, {
      role: role.id,
      policy: bucket.arn.apply(arn => JSON.stringify({
        Version: "2012-10-17",
        Statement: [{
          Effect: "Allow",
          Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"],
          Resource: [`${arn}/*`],       // no wildcards on actions — prod requirement
        }],
      })),
    }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ type: "aws:iam/rolePolicy:RolePolicy" }] });

    this.bucketArn = bucket.arn;
    this.registerOutputs({ bucketArn: this.bucketArn, dbSecretArn: this.dbSecretArn });
  }
}
```

## Step 2 — New entrypoint

```typescript
// index.ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { WebApp } from "./component";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config();
const isProd = pulumi.getStack() === "prod";

const app = new WebApp("webapp", {
  vpcId: cfg.require("vpcId"),
  subnetIds: cfg.requireObject<string[]>("subnetIds"),
  instanceType: cfg.require("instanceType"),
  nodeCount: cfg.getNumber("nodeCount"),
  dbInstanceClass: cfg.require("dbInstanceClass"),
  multiAz: isProd,
  certArn: isProd ? cfg.get("certArn") : undefined,
});

export const bucketArn = app.bucketArn;
```

```yaml
# Pulumi.dev.yaml
config:
  pkg:index:instanceType: t3.medium
  pkg:index:nodeCount: "2"
  pkg:index:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.micro
```

```yaml
# Pulumi.prod.yaml
config:
  pkg:index:instanceType: t3.large
  pkg:index:nodeCount: "4"
  pkg:index:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.medium
```

## Why Nothing Gets Replaced

| Flat URN | Aliased URN | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `…::aws:eks/cluster:Cluster::cluster` | `…:WebApp::webapp$aws:eks/cluster:Cluster::webapp-cluster` | Same resource via alias |
| *(name change)* | `webapp-cluster` vs old auto name `cluster` | Alias matches by URN chain; if old names differed, add full `aliases: [oldName]` too |

**Tips:**
- If resource names also changed (e.g., `"cluster"` → `"webapp-cluster"`), combine: `aliases: [{ name: "cluster", type: "aws:eks/cluster:Cluster" }]`.
- Run `pulumi preview` first — confirm it shows only **updates/same**, zero `replace`/`delete`. An old-alias warning means a mismatch in provider/type/name; fix before `pulumi up`.
- You can also use short-form aliasing: `{ parent: this, aliases: ["alias-type-only-is-sufficient-if-name-matches"] }` won't work here since names changed — use object form as shown.

## Safety Checklist Before `pulumi up`

1. ✅ `pulumi preview` shows `update`/`same`, never `replace`
2. ✅ Parent set to `this` on all child resources
3. ✅ Secret value already secret in state stays secret (`createSecret` keeps it encrypted at rest)
4. ✅ Prod stack untouched by dev deploys (separate stacks/state files — env isolation criterion)
5. ✅ Retain the aliases permanently — removing them later re-triggers replacement risk
